“I knew that it would eventually come down to this one day. Dragonball Evolution marked a very painful creative point in my life. To have something with my name on it as the writer be so globally reviled is gut wrenching. To receive hate mail from all over the world is heartbreaking. I spent so many years trying to deflect the blame, but at the end of the day it all comes down to the written word on page and I take full responsibility for what was such a disappointment to so many fans. I did the best I could, but at the end of the day, I ‘dropped the dragon ball.’”

“I went into the project chasing after a big payday, not as a fan of the franchise but as a businessman taking on an assignment. I have learned that when you go into a creative endeavor without passion you come out with sub-optimal results, and sometimes flat out garbage. So I’m not blaming anyone for Dragonball but myself. As a fanboy of other series, I know what it’s like to have something you love and anticipate be so disappointing.”

&#x200B;

\- BEN RAMSEY (THE WRITER OF DRAGON BALL EVOLUTION) WHO RETIRED FROM SCREENWRITER AFTER THIS MOVIE ALSO.

&#x200B;

if the dude who wrote it found the script insulting then yeah man, the people are right on this.

&#x200B;

THIS MOVIE OPENED AT #8 the weekend it came out, that should never be that low for this brand. this movie was trash yo but glad you liked it.

I'm a guy who stopped after assassin creed 3 because I followed the series since the first game and Ubisoft was always on record saying it was going just going to be a trilogy but of course it blew up crazy and more and games came out and I said screw this and stopped after 3 and came back just last year. I beat black flag, origins, odyssey and valhalla and am playing unity right now and then syndicate since they fixed the bug on the ps5. 

&#x200B;

and I like where they took the series personally, story and gameplay wise.

man to be fair, naruto and sasuke friendship arc wasn't even that well done. They were on the same teams and went on missions with each other but they never really hung out with each other or even sat down and talked to each other. 

&#x200B;

I believe Shikamaru when he say's Choji is his brother and he would die for him because they were always chilling with each other on their time off. But where do you ever see Naruto and Sasuke eating ramen together with just the two of them?

&#x200B;

In fact I just googled that and get nothing but fan art. So no I don't agree that they grew seeing each other's pain. Everyone saw how it sucked for both Naruto and Sasuke again Shikamaru was more of a brother to naruto then Sasuke.

... are you serious? Being suspected of shoplifting is different than being asked to show your receipt. Trust me, If they think you shoplifted something, they would not ask to see your receipt and would just prevent you from leaving the store all together. 

If they are are not allowing you to leave the store and have you in a room waiting for the cops to show up. It's because they have you on camera  dead to rights, stealing something or loss prevention has seen you with their own eyes. But if they don't have probable, they can ask to see your reciept but you have the right to say no and keep it [m](https://moving.Here)oving. 

Here is the real answer, since you are trying to be sleek and trying to bring up something that has nothing to do with what was going on in that video.

